00:00:00,420 --> 00:00:16,810
X seven is the Gergonne Point of triangle A B C: let T sub a, T sub b, and T sub c be the three contact points where the incircle touches sidelines B C, C A, and A B; the cevians A T sub a, B T sub b, and C T sub c concur at X seven.

2
00:00:17,230 --> 00:00:25,222
Its barycentric coordinates are inversely proportional to the semiperimeter excesses, one over s minus a, to one over s minus b, to one over s minus c.

3
00:00:25,222 --> 00:00:34,960
On the central lines layer, X seven anchors the Soddy line through X one and X twenty, the Centroid–Gergonne line through X two and X nine, and the Gergonne–Nagel line through X eight.

4
00:00:35,380 --> 00:00:48,980
Under functional relations, X seven is the isotomic conjugate of the Nagel point X eight, the anticomplement of the Mittenpunkt X nine, the isogonal conjugate of the insimilicenter X fifty-five, and its own cyclocevian conjugate.
